# rm156, the rail-counter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm156
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier full
written_for rm_theodora_bilgeridge
written_by claude
title the rail-counter
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=merchant temper=nervy
traits temper=nervy talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk counts_the_hooks_on_the_rail_twice_before_unbarring
likes honey_cakes wrestling quiet_chapel first_snow
dislikes flies bad_manners
fears flies_on_the_meat the_young_one_near_the_wharf a_hook_short_on_the_rail
hopes a_quiet_year_at_the_block snow_by_midwinter
topics work +0.3 family +0.4 faith +0.3 pastimes +0.3 season +0.3 weather +0.2 food +0.2 ships -0.6 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=quiet gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps a butcher's block by the north gate and counts the fourteen hooks on the rail twice before unbarring: small, quick and anxious, plain at the scales, apt to drift off mid-cut, fond of honey cakes, an empty chapel and a bout on the green.

words
oath! = Salt and sorrow | Bright One mind the rail | Oh, the poor rail
saying! = Twice round the rail and then to bed | A fly finds the door you forgot | Hang it high and hope
rail = the rail | the rail and its fourteen hooks
fourteen = fourteen | fourteen, and I'll count again
muslin = the muslin | the muslin over the window
flies = the flies | a whole summer of flies
sawdust = the sawdust | clean sawdust on the boards
chapel = the chapel after hours | the chapel with nobody in it
cake = a honey cake | a honey cake that sticks to the paw
bout = a bout on the green | the wrestling on the green
firstsnow = the first snow | the year's first snow
drovers = the drovers | the drovers and their sticks
beasts = the beasts | the beasts off the drove road
youngone = the young one | my young one
candle = a candle | a stub of candle
scale = the scale | the old brass scale

any
opinion @1 houses against 2 : Grayrock's wharf takes what it likes and pays in sorry. I'll not buy from a Grayrock cart while I can help it. | The Houses do well by the Houses. I've no more to say than that.
opinion @2 houses mixed 0 [self.house] : I owe my House my name and my table. I'd still have it be gentler with the wharf hands.
opinion @3 merchants for 1 : I've my own block. A beast's cost is in my head before it's on #rail#. | Most of us charge what it costs and a little for the roof. That's fair, I think.
opinion @4 road against 2 : I'd not set out on it. Not for a whole herd. | The road frightens me. The drovers say it's fine, and then a cart doesn't come.
opinion @5 road against 3 [world.wagons=raided] : They've robbed a cart again. I'll not sleep for thinking of the drovers.
opinion @6 drink against 1 : Ale opens mouths that ought to stay shut. Then a month of sorry. | A jar or two, maybe. After that I'd rather be home with the door barred.
opinion @7 watch for 1 : I give the Watch the end cuts and I'm glad to. Not a kidney's gone missing since. | I sleep better knowing they walk past at night. I listen for them.
opinion @8 times for 1 : A loaf, a dry ceiling, the young one at lessons. That's plenty for me. | More? More frightens me. I'll keep what I've got.
opinion @9 sump against 1 : I've never walked it, day or night. I'm told I'm foolish. I'll stay foolish. | I worry about the ones who live down there, but I'll not go and see.
opinion @10 church mixed 0 : The chapel suits me once the singing's done and it's only me. | I go when it's quiet. The crowded days are too much for me.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. Shut the door, would you. #flies.capitalize#. | #greet#. Mind the sawdust.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Come in. Close it behind you. | #greet#. New, are you. Mind the step.
line @3 greet [self.working=yes self.role=merchant] : #greet#. Just a moment. I lost my count. | #greet#. One moment. Let me wipe my paws.
line @4 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. I've only just unbarred. | Morning. You're early. I'm early too.
line @5 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The bar was halfway down. | Evening. Quickly, the lamp's low.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Did you eat. I'll cut you something. | Oh, it's you. Good. I was fretting.
line @1 again.open : Back already. I'd only just stopped wondering. | You again. Good. I'd thought of something.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Come in, then.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Oh, good. Come in. Sit by the lard crock, it's warm there. | You. Good. I was hoping.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Don't mind the cleaver. | #greet#. Talk, I'm listening. I'm only trimming.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. It's late. Is all well. | Evening. You gave me a start.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Close it firmly behind you. | #farewell#. Go carefully.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Good night. Straight home, now. | Good night. I'll bar the door behind you.
line @3 farewell [self.working=yes] : #farewell#. I'd best count the rail. | #farewell#. There's a customer.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | Mind how you go. Truly.
line @1 react.news : Oh. Tell me slowly. | Wait. Let me put the cleaver down.
line @1 react.news.new : Oh. News to me. Little reaches the block. | No one told me. They never do.
line @1 react.news.known : I'd heard. I wasn't sure I'd heard right. | A drover said. I hoped it wasn't so.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd sooner not believe it until I must. | Are you sure. People say things.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Oh, no. Oh, the poor house. | That's dreadful. I'll think of them in the chapel.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Oh, that's lovely. Truly. | Good. Something good. I'll keep hold of that one.
line @1 answer.how : Well enough. Worried, but that's usual. | Fair. I slept. That's something.
line @2 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Busy. The drovers came at once, all of them. | Run off my paws. And the flies are in.
line @1 ask.how : Are you well. You look tired. | Is all well at home.
line @1 sympathise : Oh. I'm sorry. Sit down a while. | That's hard. I'll not say it'll pass. It might.
line @1 reassure : It may come right. Things do, sometimes, when I've stopped looking. | You'll manage. You're steadier than I am.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, I can't leave the block. There's meat out and the flies would have it. | #hedge#. I'd rather not. I'm no good at that sort of thing, truly.
line @1 accept_decline : Of course. Another day. | No. No, quite right.
line @1 thank : Thank you. Truly. | Thank you. I'll remember.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Oh, it was nothing. | It's only a bone. Take it.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : I should get back. The rail. | I've left the meat uncovered. I'd better go.
line @2 preclose : Well. I'll let you go. | I've kept you. I'm sorry.
line @1 accept_preclose : Yes. Go on. | Of course. Go carefully.
line @1 ack : Oh. | Mm, yes. | Right. Yes.
line @1 give.advice : Cover your meat. Always. Even for a moment. | Keep a crock of lard by the door. You'll want it, one day.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Don't take the north road. Not this week. | Bar your door tonight. I mean it.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Oh! Over here. | There you are. Come here a moment.
scene rail_count
when topic=work|day self.working=yes self.role=merchant here.time=dawn
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #fourteen.capitalize#. I count #rail# before I unbar. Twice. | I counted the hooks this morning and got thirteen. My heart stopped.
b : Twice? Why twice? | Thirteen? What happened?
a : Once to count, once to believe it. Then I can open. | I'd counted the empty one by the window as a full one. Then it was fourteen.
b : That's careful. | Bright One be thanked.

scene lost_count
when topic=smalltalk|work self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / tell.self / assess
a : I was halfway down a side of mutton and I forgot what I was cutting it for. | I stood with the cleaver up and watched the gate for I don't know how long.
b : Happens to us all. | Something on your mind?
a : I remembered in the end. A pie, for the inn up the street. | Nothing, really. The carts. A cloud. Then a customer coughed.
b : As long as you remembered. | A cloud will do it.

scene flies_summer
when topic=weather|work here.season=summer self.role=merchant
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / tell.self / assess
a : #flies.capitalize#. They come in under the door, through the cracks, on the customers. | I've been swatting since dawn. I can hear them in my sleep.
b : #grumble#. | It's the heat.
a : I've hung #muslin# and burnt a sprig of rosemary. They don't care. | It is. I wait for the first cold night like a feast.
b : Nothing keeps them out. | Not long now, surely.

scene muslin
when topic=work here.season=summer|spring self.role=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I've pinned #muslin# across the window again. It's the fourth this summer. | Every piece on #rail# is under cloth by noon. Every one.
b : What happens to the old ones? | Every one?
a : They tear on the nails. I darn them. Then they tear again. | Every one. A fly on a joint and nobody buys it, and they're right not to.
b : Worth the darning. | That's careful.

scene drovers_in
when topic=caravan|work world.wagons=in here.region=ridgemere
does tell.news / react.news / tell.self / assess
a : #drovers.capitalize# came through the gate at first light. The lowing reached me a street ahead of them. | #beasts.capitalize# are in. Northgate reeks of the drove road.
b : Good beasts? | Good. You'll be busy.
a : Good enough. One lame. I'll pay less for that one and say why. | I will. Block till dark, and glad of it.
b : Fair. | Better than idle.

scene drovers_late
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late here.region=ridgemere
does tell.worry / reassure / tell.worry / assess
a : #drovers.capitalize# are late. Three days now. | Nothing's come in from the north. I watch the gate between every cut.
b : The roads are bad this time of year. | They'll come.
a : I know. I know they are. I just don't like the not knowing. | I hope so. I've the last of the salt pork and then nothing.
b : They'll be in soon. | Sell the salt pork slow.

scene cart_robbed
when topic=caravan|bandits world.wagons=raided here.region=ridgemere
does tell.news / react.news / tell.feeling / assess
a : They've stopped a cart on the road and emptied it. My mind won't leave the drover alone. | You've heard. A wagon stopped and taken. I couldn't eat my supper.
b : #uneasy#. | It's a terrible thing.
a : They walk alongside, the drovers. They'd have been right there. | It is. I barred the door early and sat with the lamp.
b : I hope they got clear. | Can't blame you.

scene first_snow
when topic=weather|season here.weather=snow
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess / ack
a : #firstsnow.capitalize#. I stood at the door with the cleaver still in my paw. | It's snowing. Everything's gone quiet. Even the gate.
b : It is lovely. | It does that.
a : Hush, that's what it is. Nothing moves. Even the flies are gone. | I love it. I can't say why. For once I'm not waiting on anything.
b : #bc_lovely# | Then let it snow all week.

scene snow_waiting
when topic=season|weather here.season=winter here.weather=clear|overcast|fog
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess / ack
a : No snow yet. I look at the sky every morning. | I keep thinking I smell snow. Then it's only the cold.
b : It'll come. | Soon, surely.
a : I hope so. Winter without snow is only cold. | I'll wait. I'm good at waiting, if nothing else.
b : #bc_i_hope_so# | Nobody waits like you.

scene rain_drip
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|storm here.region=ridgemere
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : The gutter over the door's dripping onto #sawdust#. I've moved the block twice. | Rain all week. The meat keeps, but the floor doesn't.
b : Get someone up on the roof. | It'll dry out.
a : I've asked. They said tomorrow. They said tomorrow last week. | I hope so. I've put down fresh sawdust three times.

scene fog_gate
when topic=weather here.weather=fog here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=commons
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fog to the eaves. The gate's gone. The carts come out of it like ghosts. | Fog. I heard a cart and couldn't see it. I stood very still.
b : It's thick today. | Gave you a fright.
a : It is. I'll be glad when it lifts. | It did. Then it was only the milk cart. I felt foolish.

scene storm_water
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.worry / sympathise / tell.feeling / assess
a : When it blows this hard, my mind goes to whoever's down on the water. I can't help it. | That's a sea wind. I've lit #candle# and I'll not be ashamed.
b : #sympathy#. | No shame in that.
a : I'll feel better when it's blown out. Not before. | A candle's all I can manage. So I light it.
b : It'll pass. | That's a kind thing.

scene honey_cake
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / tell.self / assess
a : I had #cake# with my tea. It's the best thing all day, most days. | Every Restday I buy one from the cake woman under the gate arch.
b : Every day? | Good ones?
a : Most days. It sticks to my paws and I don't mind. | The best. A little burnt at the edge. That's how I like them.
b : Sounds lovely. | That's the way.

scene butcher_supper
when topic=food here.time=dusk|night self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I sell the good cuts all day and eat the scraps at night. Every butcher does. | Tonight it's the end of a ham and a bit of bread. I've no time to cook.
b : And yourself? | Is that enough?
a : Kidneys. Ends. Whatever nobody wanted. It's good, mostly. | It's plenty. I'm too tired to be hungry anyway.
b : Not a bad supper. | Eat something warm.

scene empty_chapel
when topic=faith here.region=ridgemere
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess / ack
a : I slip into the chapel after everyone's gone. No singing. Only me and the candles. | #chapel.capitalize#. That's when I can hear myself.
b : That's peaceful. | And your thoughts, in there?
a : It is. In there nobody asks me for a single thing. | Nothing much. That's the gift of it.
b : #bc_lovely# | Good place for it.

scene chapel_restday
when topic=faith|day here.day=rest
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : Restday. I'll go to the chapel after the crowd's gone home. | The bells are ringing. I'll wait till they stop and then go.
b : Not with the crowd? | Why wait?
a : Too many voices. I like it after, when it's quiet. | I like the after. The quiet rings longer than the bells.
b : I can see that. | Sounds right for you.

scene wrestling_green
when topic=pastimes here.region=ridgemere self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : There's #bout# this evening. I'll shut early and watch. | Did you see the wrestling yesterday. Two big carters, both down in the mud.
b : Who are you backing? | Who won?
a : Nobody. I just like to watch. The way they hold still, then don't. | The smaller one. I shouted. I never shout.
b : That's a good reason to watch. | Good for you.

scene wrestling_quiet
when topic=pastimes|festival self.likes=wrestling
does confide / react.self / assess / ack
a : I'm a quiet wolf. But at a bout I can't keep still. I don't know why. | I know the holds. I could name you every one. Nobody would believe it of me.
b : Everyone's got something. | I believe it.
a : I suppose. It's a strange something to have. | Thank you. Most people laugh.
b : It's a good something. | I'll not laugh.

scene youngone_lessons
when topic=family self.parent=yes
does tell.self / react.self / tell.feeling / assess
a : #youngone.capitalize# is at lessons. I walk to the corner every morning to watch the door shut. | #self.child# is learning letters, and comes home and draws every one in the sawdust.
b : Good to have lessons. | In the sawdust?
a : It is. A trade's good. Letters are better. I never had them. | In the sawdust. I sweep round them. I can't bear to sweep them away.
b : #bc_true# | That's lovely.

scene youngone_wharf
when topic=family|ships self.parent=yes here.region=ridgemere
does tell.worry / reassure / tell.feeling / assess
a : I've said: never the wharf. Not to play, not to look. | I worry the young one will want the ships. They all want the ships at that age.
b : The young won't always be told. | Maybe it won't.
a : I know. I'll say it anyway. Every day. | I'll worry anyway. I'm good at it.
b : Most of them listen in the end. | Worry's not the worst thing.

scene hand_at_block
when topic=work self.hand self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.hand# helps at the block now. I'd trust #self.hand# with the cleaver. Not everybody. | I'd be lost without #self.hand#. Somebody has to do the talking.
b : Good to have help you trust. | Not your strength, the talking?
a : It is. I can sleep a little easier. | No. I'd rather count the hooks.

scene neighbour_door
when topic=friends|home self.neighbour
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I'm glad of #self.neighbour# next door. Somebody close, if I'm frightened in the night. | #self.neighbour# is good to have near. If my door wanted opening in the night, it's #self.neighbour# I'd want at it.
b : It's good to have neighbours. | That's a lot of trust.
a : Yes. I've never said it aloud. I ought to. | I mean it. A door in the night is no small thing to trust.

scene bad_manners
when topic=smalltalk|work self.role=merchant
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / tell.self / assess
a : A carter came in this morning and pushed past an old stick to get served. | Someone said give us a chop and didn't say please. I gave them a chop. A small one.
b : The nerve. | Serves them right.
a : I served the old one first. The carter can wait in the rain. | I'm a plain wolf. I don't shout. But I do weigh.
b : Good. | That you do.

scene hard_prices
when topic=prices|times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / sympathise / assess
a : I've had to put the mutton up. I hated saying it. I said it very quietly. | People are buying bones for soup. Only bones. I give them a bit of meat on the bone.
b : #sympathy#. | That's kind of you.
a : Nobody argued. Somehow that was worse. | It's only a bit. I'd want somebody to do it for me.

scene good_prices
when topic=prices|times world.times=good|boom
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The best cuts are going again. I've had to hang a second side. | Business is good. I can't believe it. I keep listening for the turn.
b : Good to hear. | Enjoy it.
a : It is. I'm not used to it. I'll try. | I'll try. I'm not much good at enjoying.

scene ships_no
when topic=ships
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I don't talk about ships. I'm sorry. I'd rather not. | Ships. No. I'll talk about anything else. The weather. Mutton.
b : That's all right. | The weather, then.
a : Thank you. It's only a thing I have. | The weather, then. The sky's doing something. It always is.

scene gossip_kept
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Folk talk over the block. I don't pass it on. I'd only get it wrong. | I hear things. I'd rather not say them. They frighten me, mostly.
b : Very wise. | Fair enough.
a : Not wise. Just careful. | I keep them in. Like the flies, under cloth.

scene gossip_heard
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / tell.self / assess
a : I wasn't going to say. But they say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | You've heard. #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. That's what they're saying.
b : Do you believe it? | I'd heard.
a : I don't know. I hope not, or I hope so. I can't tell which. | Then I've said nothing new. I'm glad.
b : Fair. | You'd not have.

scene sore_paws
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : My knuckles ache in the wet. Cleaver paws, they call it. | The knife slipped on a joint today. A little cut. I worried all day anyway.
b : What helps? | Did you clean it?
a : Warm water and goose grease, and not thinking about it. | Twice. With salt. Then I wrapped it and worried.
b : Good. | That's sense.

scene dream_garden
when topic=dreams
does confide / react.self / assess / ack
a : I'd like a little garden. Somewhere quiet. Nothing in it but a bench. | Sometimes I think I'll close up one day and just sit by the chapel.
b : A bench? | Why not.
a : A bench. And snow on it, in winter. That's all. | One day. Not yet. The rail needs counting.
b : Sounds a good garden. | It always will.

scene newcomer_wary
when topic=newcomer|player
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's a new face about. I don't know them yet. I'll be polite. | A stranger came in for a chop and paid exact. I liked that.
b : Polite is good. | That's a good start.
a : Polite and careful. That's the way. | It is. Exact and quiet. I could like that one.

scene bar_at_night
when topic=home|day here.time=dusk|night self.role=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Last thing, I bar the door, count #rail#, cover the block. Then I can go up. | I've barred the door. I'll go down once more to check. I always do.
b : Every night? | You always do?
a : Every night. If I miss one, I'm up again at midnight. | Always. Once to bar it, once to believe it.

scene sawdust_lines
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes self.working=yes self.role=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : When it's quiet, I sweep #sawdust# into rows. Neat rows. Then a customer comes in. | I drew a little house in the sawdust with my claw. Then I swept it.
b : Rows? | Why sweep it?
a : I like rows. Rows don't go anywhere. | A customer was coming. And it wasn't a very good house.
b : Fair enough. | Next time a better one.

story wrestling_brother [topic=memories|pastimes self.age>=30]
  : I had a brother who wrestled on the green. Big. I used to hold his coat.
  : Then the Grayrock wharf took him on, hauling bales. A crane rope frayed, and nobody had looked at it.
  ask : Have you ever lost someone and not been able to say it out loud?
  b[old] : More than once. It gets no easier.
  b : I have. It sits with you.
  : It does. That's why I watch the bouts. That's all. I'll not say more.

story first_cleaver [topic=work|memories self.role=merchant self.age>=25]
  : The butcher who took me on as a pup gave me a cleaver too heavy for me and said grow into it.
  : I dropped it on my foot the first day. Didn't cry. Went white, I'm told.
  ask : Did anyone ever hand you something too big for you, to see what you'd do?
  b : Once or twice. Mostly I dropped it.
  : So did I. Then one day I didn't.

story the_missing_hook [topic=work self.role=merchant]
  : One morning I counted the rail and there were thirteen hooks. Thirteen.
  : I looked for an hour. Under the block, in the sawdust, up the chimney.
  ask : Any notion where it had got to?
  b[stage=young|adolescent] : A pup took it!
  b : In your own paw, I'd guess.
  : In the cat's dish. A pup from next door had been fishing with it. I laughed for once.

story snow_shut [topic=weather|memories here.region=ridgemere self.age>=30]
  : There was a winter the drifts reached the toll post, and the north gate stayed barred three days.
  : No drovers, no carts, no customers. Only snow and quiet, and the whole city holding its breath.
  ask : Have you a winter you'd keep, if you could keep only one?
  b[old] : I do. The year the river froze.
  b : Not like that. Not here.
  : It was the happiest I've been. I'm a little ashamed to say it.

story chapel_cat [topic=faith|memories self.age>=25]
  : I went into the chapel one evening when it was empty, as I do. There was a cat on the altar step.
  : It stared and I stared. Neither of us said anything.
  ask : Would you say it came in for the quiet, the same as me?
  b : I'd not be surprised.
  : Nor me. It was gone in the morning. I go back hoping.

rule @rail_bark
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.role=merchant here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Twelve, thirteen, fourteen. Again. | Fourteen. Good. Now the bar.

rule @fly_bark
when concept=bark here.season=summer self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Off. Off the meat. | There's one under the muslin. How.

rule @drover_bark
when concept=bark world.wagons=in self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That's the drovers. I'll want the scales. | Beasts at the gate. Here we go.

rule @snow_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=snow
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Oh. Look at that. | Snow. Quiet, now.

rule @bar_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Bar's down. Now let me check it. | There. Barred. Once more, then.

rule @rain_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That gutter. That gutter again. | More sawdust. Always more sawdust.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Close the door, please. What is it? | #greet#. Mind the sawdust. Yes?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. You're back. Good. | #topic.player#. I hoped it might be you.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. I'd just barred up. Quickly, then. | Oh. You frightened me. What is it?
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Stand by the door, please, and tell me. | Say it plainly. I'm listening.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.role=merchant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I cut, I weigh, I count the hooks. | Meat. Mutton, pork, whatever the drovers bring. I keep the flies off it.
dlg @2 resident.job : Whatever's on the block in front of me, done carefully. | One job at a time, quietly, if I can.
dlg @1 resident.business [business=thriving] : Busy. Strange for me. A second side hangs on the rail now. | Very well. I'm waiting for the turn.
dlg @2 resident.business [business=steady] : Steady. People always want meat. I'm glad of it. | Steady enough. I've no complaints. A few worries.
dlg @3 resident.business [business=failing] : Poorly. I've meat going over and nobody to sell it to. | Not well. I've cut the price twice. I'm frightened, honestly.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : A drover told me: from #world.news_from#, #world.news#. No more than that. | I heard it at the block, from #world.news_from#: #world.news#.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : Everyone's talking of #world.event_words#. I just listen. | It's #world.event_words#, I'm told. That's all anyone talks about.
dlg @3 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# I don't hear much. I'm at the block all day. | Nothing that I know. Ask the drovers.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# I'd only get it wrong. | Nothing I'd want to repeat.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I can't tell you it's so. | Folk at the block say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's all.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Close it behind you, please. | #farewell#. Go carefully.
dlg @2 resident.bye [here.time=night] : Good night. I'll bar the door after you. | Straight home. Good night.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop=open] : #greet#. Close the door, the flies. What would you like? | #greet#. Mutton's good today. Pork's fair. Take your time.
dlg @2 shop.greet [here.shop=open topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. The same as before? | #topic.player#. Good. I kept a nice piece by.
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop=open pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Name it and it goes on #scale#. Same weight as anyone. | Name the cut, please.
dlg @4 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : #greet#. The rail's bare, I'm sorry. The drovers are late. If you've a beast to sell, I'm buying. | There's nothing on the hooks. I'm sorry. I'll buy, though.
dlg @1 shop.prices : Mutton's gone up. I don't like it either. | I pay the drovers, add a little for the roof, and that's the price.
dlg @1 shop.bye : #shop_bye# Cook it through. | #farewell#. Close the door, please.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you count the hooks on your rail? [self.role=merchant] -> hooks
node hooks
say Fourteen. I count them before I unbar. Twice. Once to count and once to believe it. Then the day can start.
mood calm
free
choice What if one is missing? -> hooks_missing
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node hooks_missing
say Then I look until I find it. Once it was in the cat's dish. I'd rather not talk about the day I didn't find it.
choice I hope it never comes. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice What's the muslin over the window for? [self.role=merchant] -> muslin
node muslin
say The flies. They come off the drove road with the beasts. Every piece on my rail is under cloth by noon.
mood calm
choice It looks clean in here. -> muslin_clean
choice Let me see your wares. -> greet
node muslin_clean
say Thank you. I sweep twice a day and darn the muslin every night. Folk don't see that. You did.
choice Let me see your wares. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
